GFiZWwyNzkwOTgwODI=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:gdscript","name":"topic:gdscript","color":"ffee88","default":false,"description":"","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":2,"created_at":"2025-07-11T19:16:23Z","updated_at":"2025-07-12T16:07:47Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"MEMBER","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\n4.5 beta3 and earlier\n\n### System information\n\nW10\n\n### Issue description\n\nWhen you do\n```GDScript\n@onready var node = get_node()\n```\nyou will get this warning-error:\n```\nError at (5, 1): The default value uses \"get_node()\" which won't return nodes in the scene tree before \"_ready()\" is called. Use the \"@onready\" annotation to solve this. (Warning treated as error.)\n```\nHowever it does not appear for every method that also requires node to be ready:\n- `get_node_or_null()`\n- `get_child()`\n- `get_children()`\n- `get_parent()`\n- `find_child()`\n- `find_children()`\n- `find_parent()`\n- `has_node()`\n- `owner`.\n(also possibly `get_index()`)\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n1. Use any of the above methods to assign default value without `@onready`.\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\nN/A","closed_by":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/108532/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/108532/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null}